### Sample requests for all three services.
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (or Visual Studio) and click "Send Request".

@analytics = http://localhost:5100
@aihub = http://localhost:5200

### ---------- Insights.Analytics ----------

### Whether Neo4j holds a loaded knowledge model and PostgreSQL answers, with the business dates the data covers
GET {{analytics}}/health

### The whole knowledge model from Neo4j: tables and columns, concepts, relationships, metrics, business rules, examples
GET {{analytics}}/schema

### The part of the knowledge model one question is about (what the AI Hub puts in its prompt)
POST {{analytics}}/context
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?"
}

### A follow-up keeps the earlier question's concepts
POST {{analytics}}/context
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "and only on Thursday?",
  "history": ["Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?"]
}

### The last knowledge model load (it loads at startup and whenever knowledge-model.json, business-rules.json or query-examples.json changes)
GET {{analytics}}/knowledge-model/status

### Load the knowledge model files into Neo4j again
POST {{analytics}}/knowledge-model/reload

### Run a read-only SQL query on PostgreSQL
POST {{analytics}}/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT str_num AS store, round(sum(amount), 2) AS net_sales FROM public.pos_basket_line GROUP BY str_num ORDER BY net_sales DESC LIMIT 5"
}

### Anything but a single SELECT over the knowledge model's tables is rejected with 400
POST {{analytics}}/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "DELETE FROM public.pos_basket_line"
}

### ---------- AI through Insights.Analytics (clients only need {{analytics}}) ----------

### Whole question in one call: SQL, rows and plain-English answer
POST {{analytics}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?"
}

### English question -> SQL (forwarded to Insights.AiHub)
POST {{analytics}}/ai/sql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?"
}

### AI Hub status and model
GET {{analytics}}/ai/health

### ---------- Insights.AiHub directly (same endpoints Insights.Analytics forwards to) ----------

### 1. English question -> SQL (the AI Hub gets the question's knowledge model context from {{analytics}}/context)
POST {{aihub}}/sql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?"
}

### 2. Run the returned SQL with POST {{analytics}}/query, then send the question + results here
POST {{aihub}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?",
  "sql": "SELECT str_num AS store, round(sum(amount), 2) AS net_sales FROM public.pos_basket_line GROUP BY str_num ORDER BY net_sales DESC LIMIT 5",
  "results": {
    "columns": ["store", "net_sales"],
    "rows": [{ "store": 101, "net_sales": 152340.55 }],
    "truncated": false
  }
}

### OpenAI tokens and estimated cost so far
GET {{aihub}}/usage

### Which service a question is for: "analytics" (the sales data), "db-guide" (the database's structure) or "unclear"
POST {{aihub}}/intent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which table holds product prices?" }

### One question, answered by whichever service it's for (Analytics or DB Guide POST /ask, passed through in "result")
POST {{aihub}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?" }

### A follow-up: each earlier turn says its intent, and what answered it (sql from Analytics, answer from DB Guide)
POST {{aihub}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "and the lowest?",
  "history": [
    { "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?", "intent": "analytics", "sql": "SELECT ..." }
  ]
}

### Up to three questions to ask next, after an answer
POST {{aihub}}/follow-ups
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?", "intent": "analytics", "answer": "Store 12 had the highest net sales.", "columns": ["store", "net_sales"] }

### ---------- Insights.Workspace (each user's schedules and board widgets; normally reached through the gateway) ----------

@workspace = http://localhost:5400

### The user's schedules, with when each would next run
GET {{workspace}}/schedules
X-User: Admin

### Save a schedule (not run yet)
POST {{workspace}}/schedules
X-User: Admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Top stores", "question": "Which 5 stores had the highest net sales?", "frequency": "weekly", "dayOfWeek": 1, "time": "08:00", "startsOn": "2026-11-02", "board": "basket-intelligence" }

### The widgets on a board
GET {{workspace}}/widgets?board=basket-intelligence
X-User: Admin

### ---------- Insights.DbGuide (questions about a database's structure, from its catalog in Neo4j) ----------

@dbguide = http://localhost:5300

### Whether the catalog is loaded in Neo4j and the AI Hub answers
GET {{dbguide}}/health

### The whole catalog: database, business areas, tables in brief, every join with its SQL condition
GET {{dbguide}}/catalog

### One table in full, with its documentation page
GET {{dbguide}}/catalog/tables/inventory.Products

### The part of the catalog one question is about (what the AI Hub is given)
POST {{dbguide}}/context
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "How do I join order items to products?"
}

### Whole question in one call: answer, tables used and an example query
POST {{dbguide}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Which table should I use for product data?"
}

### A follow-up builds on the earlier question and its answer
POST {{dbguide}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "and how do I get its supplier?",
  "history": [{ "question": "Which table should I use for product data?", "answer": "Use inventory.Products." }]
}

### The last catalog load (it loads at startup and whenever a file in catalog/ or db-guide.json changes)
GET {{dbguide}}/catalog/status

### Load the catalog export into Neo4j again
POST {{dbguide}}/catalog/reload
